IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-worker`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) -- the seat of the person conducting a business or undertaking (the PCBU): a
-- non-Commonwealth licensee, a Commonwealth company or a public authority that engages workers, asked as its owner or
-- manager would ask it. (The Commonwealth itself is also a PCBU under s 12(1)(a); it gets no seat, being the
-- government, but the answers here are the same for it.) "Must I report this incident to Comcare, and how? Must I leave the site alone? Must I consult my workers?
-- What can I do when a worker stops work? What is the most I can be fined?"
--
-- Every question below calls a rule in whs-worker.l4 and restates none: the notifiable incident (ss 35 to 37), the
-- consultation duty (ss 47 to 49), the penalties (ss 30A to 33, Schedule 4). The duties that are the PCBU's alone and
-- that whs-worker.l4 does not ask -- notifying (s 38), keeping the record (s 38(7)), preserving the site (s 39), directing
-- alternative work (s 87) -- are encoded here.
--
-- Edition, scope and the penalty caveat: see whs-worker.l4 and NOTES.md. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- the PCBU's questions`

§§ `s 38 -- must I notify Comcare` -- arises only if an incident has happened

-- s 38(1): "A person who conducts a business or undertaking must ensure that the regulator is notified immediately after
-- becoming aware that a notifiable incident arising out of the conduct of the business or undertaking has occurred."
-- Penalty: tier D ($14,000 for an individual, $70,000 for a body corporate, Schedule 4 cl 2, before indexation). (2): "by
-- the fastest possible means". (3): "(a) by telephone; or (b) in writing". (4): by telephone, with the details asked
-- and, if required, "a written notice of the incident within 48 hours of that requirement being made". s 4: the
-- regulator is Comcare.
DECLARE `Notifying Comcare` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must ensure Comcare is notified immediately after I become aware of it, by the fastest possible means, by telephone or in writing, and in writing within 48 hours if Comcare asks (s 38(1) to (4)); I must keep a record of it for at least 5 years (s 38(7))`
    `no: it is not a notifiable incident arising out of my business or undertaking`

@export Must I notify Comcare of this incident, and how (ss 35 to 38)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened` @desc The most serious thing that happened: a death, an injury or illness needing the treatment listed, a dangerous incident listed in s 37, or something else
      `the regulations exclude it, or add it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Work Health and Safety Regulations exclude this kind of injury, illness or incident, or add it to the list, reversing the answer the Act gives (not encoded: false unless you know otherwise)
      `it arose out of my business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it arose out of the conduct of your business or undertaking
GIVETH A `Notifying Comcare`
`Must I notify Comcare` MEANS
    IF `Is it a notifiable incident` `what happened` `the regulations exclude it, or add it` `it arose out of my business or undertaking`
    THEN `yes: I must ensure Comcare is notified immediately after I become aware of it, by the fastest possible means, by telephone or in writing, and in writing within 48 hours if Comcare asks (s 38(1) to (4)); I must keep a record of it for at least 5 years (s 38(7))`
    ELSE `no: it is not a notifiable incident arising out of my business or undertaking`

-- s 38(7): "keep a record of each notifiable incident for at least 5 years from the day that notice of the incident is
-- given to the regulator". Penalty: tier F ($7,000 for an individual, $35,000 for a body corporate, before indexation).
-- Read as up to and including the same date five years on.
@export Until what day must I keep the record of a notifiable incident (s 38(7))?
GIVEN `the day I notified Comcare` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the incident was given to Comcare
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when must I keep the incident record` MEANS `add years` `the day I notified Comcare` 5

-- s 39(1): "The person with management or control of a workplace at which a notifiable incident has occurred must ensure
-- so far as is reasonably practicable, that the site where the incident occurred is not disturbed until an inspector
-- arrives at the site or any earlier time that an inspector directs." Penalty: tier D. (2): the site includes any plant,
-- substance, structure or thing associated with it. (3): it "does not prevent any action: (a) to assist an injured
-- person; or (b) to remove a deceased person; or (c) that is essential to make the site safe or to minimise the risk of a
-- further notifiable incident; or (d) that is associated with a police investigation; or (e) for which an inspector or the
-- regulator has given permission."
DECLARE `Action at the site` IS ONE OF
    `assisting an injured person`
    `removing a deceased person`
    `what is essential to make the site safe or minimise the risk of a further notifiable incident`
    `something associated with a police investigation`
    `something an inspector or Comcare has permitted`
    `anything else, such as cleaning up or resuming work`

DECLARE `Disturbing the site` IS ONE OF
    `yes: s 39(3) allows this action`
    `yes: an inspector has arrived, or directed that the site may be disturbed`
    `no: I must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, that the site is not disturbed until an inspector arrives or directs otherwise (s 39(1))`
    `s 39 does not bind me: I do not manage or control the workplace`

@export May the site of a notifiable incident at my workplace be disturbed (s 39)?
GIVEN `I manage or control the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your business or undertaking manages or controls, wholly or partly, the workplace where the notifiable incident happened
      `an inspector has arrived or directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an inspector has arrived at the site, or has directed an earlier time
      `the action` IS AN `Action at the site` @desc What you want to do at the site, or to the plant, substance, structure or thing involved
GIVETH A `Disturbing the site`
`May the incident site be disturbed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I manage or control the workplace`)
    THEN `s 39 does not bind me: I do not manage or control the workplace`
    ELSE IF `an inspector has arrived or directed otherwise`
         THEN `yes: an inspector has arrived, or directed that the site may be disturbed`
         ELSE IF `the action` EQUALS `anything else, such as cleaning up or resuming work`
              THEN `no: I must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, that the site is not disturbed until an inspector arrives or directs otherwise (s 39(1))`
              ELSE `yes: s 39(3) allows this action`

§§ `ss 47 to 49 -- must I consult my workers`

DECLARE `Consulting my workers` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must consult them, so far as is reasonably practicable: share the information, let them give their views and contribute, take the views into account and tell them the outcome (ss 47, 48(1)); penalty tier C`
    `yes: I must consult them, and their health and safety representative must be involved (ss 47, 48(2)); penalty tier C`
    `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or these workers are not directly affected by it`

@export Must I consult my workers about this safety matter (ss 47 to 49)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Safety matter` @desc What you are doing or deciding about health and safety
      `the workers are, or are likely to be, directly affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the workers are, or are likely to be, directly affected by the matter
      `the workers have a health and safety representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the workers' work group has a health and safety representative
GIVETH A `Consulting my workers`
`Must I consult my workers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the consultation the s 47 duty needs` `the matter` `the workers are, or are likely to be, directly affected` `the workers have a health and safety representative`
    WHEN `yes: the business must consult me, so far as is reasonably practicable, sharing the information, letting me give my views and contribute, taking them into account and telling me the outcome (ss 47, 48(1))`
         THEN `yes: I must consult them, so far as is reasonably practicable: share the information, let them give their views and contribute, take the views into account and tell them the outcome (ss 47, 48(1)); penalty tier C`
    WHEN `yes: the business must consult me through my health and safety representative, who must be involved (ss 47, 48(2))`
         THEN `yes: I must consult them, and their health and safety representative must be involved (ss 47, 48(2)); penalty tier C`
    OTHERWISE `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or these workers are not directly affected by it`

§§ `ss 84 to 88 -- when a worker stops work` -- arises only if a worker has ceased unsafe work

-- s 87: "If a worker ceases work under this Division, the person conducting the business or undertaking may direct the
-- worker to carry out suitable alternative work at the same or another workplace if that work is safe and appropriate for
-- the worker to carry out until the worker can resume normal duties."
@export A worker has stopped unsafe work: may I direct them to do other work (s 87)?
GIVEN `the worker ceased work under s 84 or on an HSR's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker ceased or refused work under s 84, or on a health and safety representative's direction under s 85
      `the other work is suitable, safe and appropriate for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the alternative work, at the same or another workplace, is suitable and is safe and appropriate for that worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I direct alternative work` IF
        `the worker ceased work under s 84 or on an HSR's direction`
    AND `the other work is suitable, safe and appropriate for them`

§§ `ss 30A to 33, Schedule 4 -- the most I can be fined`

@export What is the most my business, or I as its owner or officer, can be fined or imprisoned for a breach of a health and safety duty (ss 30A to 33, Schedule 4)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc Which offence: industrial manslaughter, category 1 (negligent or reckless conduct exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury), category 2 (a failure that exposes someone to that risk) or category 3 (any failure)
      `the business is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate (a company or other corporation) rather than you as an individual conducting the business, or as its officer
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty`
`What is the most the business can be fined` MEANS
    IF `the business is a body corporate`
    THEN `the maximum penalty` `the offence` `a body corporate`
    ELSE `the maximum penalty` `the offence` `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it`
